bon?&quot;,&quot;6&quot;],[&quot;What instrument is used to look at distant stars and planets?&quot;,&quot;Telescope&quot;],[&quot;What is the process by which rocks are broken down by weather and climate?&quot;,&quot;Weathering&quot;],[&quot;What is the main metal found in liquid thermometers?&quot;,&quot;Mercury&quot;],[&quot;Which scientist discovered penicillin?&quot;,&quot;Alexander Fleming&quot;],[&quot;What is the term for a male honeybee?&quot;,&quot;Drone&quot;],[&quot;What is the boiling point of water in Fahrenheit?&quot;,&quot;212 degrees Fahrenheit&quot;],[&quot;What subatomic particle carries a negative electrical charge?&quot;,&quot;Electron&quot;],[&quot;What is the common name for the larynx?&quot;,&quot;Voice box&quot;],[&quot;What is the term for molten rock beneath the Earth&#39;s surface?&quot;,&quot;Magma&quot;],[&quot;What is the smallest unit of life?&quot;,&quot;Cell&quot;],[&quot;Which vitamin is essential for blood clotting?&quot;,&quot;Vitamin K&quot;],[&quot;What gas is released when baking soda reacts with vinegar?&quot;,&quot;Carbon dioxide&quot;],[&quot;What is the name of the nearest star to Earth (other than the Sun)?&quot;,&quot;Proxima Centauri&quot;],[&quot;What is the process of cell division that results in four daughter cells each with half the number of chromosomes?&quot;,&quot;Meiosis&quot;],[&quot;What term describes animals that maintain a constant body temperature?&quot;,&quot;Endotherm or warm-blooded&quot;],[&quot;What is the chemical symbol for sodium?&quot;,&quot;Na&quot;],[&quot;What is the primary function of white blood cells?&quot;,&quot;To fight infections and defend the body against pathogens&quot;],[&quot;What is the name of the boundary between the crust and the mantle?&quot;,&quot;Mohorovičić discontinuity (Moho)&quot;],[&quot;What unit is used to measure electrical resistance?&quot;,&quot;Ohm&quot;],[&quot;What is the most common isotope of hydrogen?&quot;,&quot;Protium&quot;],[&quot;What type of lens is thi