            <div placeholder="Title Here" class="resizable" style="font-size: 45.8333px; font-weight: bold; width: 341.01px; text-align: left; height: 72px; cursor: default;" data-original-value="Question:">Question:</div></div><div class="element-container bg-transparent hide-controls multi-select" data-type="text" style="left: 15px; top: 87px; z-index: 218;" data-merge-source-id="src_1785739640011" data-merge-col="0" data-merge-data="[&quot;What is the chemical symbol for gold?&quot;,&quot;What planet is known as the Red Planet?&quot;,&quot;What gas do plants absorb from the atmosphere for photosynthesis?&quot;,&quot;What is the powerhouse of the cell?&quot;,&quot;What is the hardest natural substance on Earth?&quot;,&quot;What force keeps objects tied to the Earth?&quot;,&quot;What is the center of an atom called?&quot;,&quot;What is the speed of light in a vacuum (approximate)?&quot;,&quot;What vitamin do we get primarily from sunlight?&quot;,&quot;What is the largest organ in the human body?&quot;,&quot;How many bones are in the adult human body?&quot;,&quot;What is the most abundant gas in Earth's atmosphere?&quot;,&quot;What instrument is used to measure earthquakes?&quot;,&quot;What is the chemical formula for water?&quot;,&quot;Who proposed the theory of general relativity?&quot;,&quot;What is the process of a liquid turning into a gas called?&quot;,&quot;What type of animal is a whale?&quot;,&quot;What is the freezing point of water in Celsius?&quot;,&quot;What part of the plant conducts photosynthesis?&quot;,&quot;What is the pH of pure water?&quot;,&quot;What blood type is known as the universal donor?&quot;,&quot;What galaxy is Earth located in?&quot;,&quot;What is the study of weather called?&quot;,&quot;What is the chemical symbol for iron?&quot;,&quot;What is the primary source of energy for Earth's climate system?&quot;,&quot;What do you call an animal that eats both plants and meat?&quot;,&quot;What is the largest planet in our solar system?&quot;,&quot;What is the atomic number of carbon?&quot;,&quot;What instrument is used to look at distant stars and planets?&quot;,&quot;What is the process by which rocks are broken down by weather and climate?&quot;,&quot;What is the main metal found in liquid thermometers?&quot;,&quot;Which scientist discovered penicillin?&quot;,&quot;What is the term for a male honeybee?&quot;,&quot;What is the boiling point of water in Fahrenheit?&quot;,&quot;What subatomic particle carries a negative electrical charge?&quot;,&quot;What is the common name for the larynx?&quot;,&quot;What is the term for molten rock beneath the Earth's surface?&quot;,&quot;What is the smallest unit of life?&quot;,&quot;Which vitamin is essential for blood clotting?&quot;,&quot;What gas is released when baking soda reacts with vinegar?&quot;,&quot;What is the name of the nearest star to Earth (other than the Sun)?&quot;,&quot;What is the process of cell division that results in four daughter cells each with half the number of chromosomes?&quot;,&quot;What term describes animals that maintain a constant body temperature?&quot;,&quot;What is the chemical symbol for sodium?&quot;,&quot;What is the primary function of white blood cells?&quot;,&quot;What is the name of the boundary between the crust and the mantle?&quot;,&quot;What unit is used to measure electrical resistance?&quot;,&quot;What is the most common isotope of hydrogen?&quot;,&quot;What type of lens is thicker in the middle than at the edges?&quot;,&quot;What is the term for the total mass of living matter in a given area?&quot;]"><div class="controls ui-control popover-nw" contenteditable="false" data-offset-x="0" data-offset-y="0" style="margin-left: 0px; margin-top: 0px; display: none;">
